WEBVTT

00:00:08.110 --> 00:00:14.300
Mobile Suit Zeta Gundam

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:22.680
aoku nemuru mizu no hoshi ni sotto

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:22.680
Kissing softly the star of water that sleeps in blue,

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:31.410
kuchizuke shite inochi no hi wo tomosu hito yo

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:31.410
A person who lights the fire of life,

00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:36.300
toki to iu kin'iro no sazanami wa

00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:36.300
The time, the golden ripple,

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:45.070
oozora no kuchibiru ni umareta toiki ne

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:45.070
is a sigh from the lips of the sky,

00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:49.300
kokoro ni uzumoreta

00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:49.300
The stars of kindness...

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:52.270
yasashisa no hoshitachi ga

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:52.270
...buried in heart flame up...

00:00:52.270 --> 00:00:56.440
honoo age yobiau

00:00:52.270 --> 00:00:56.440
...and call to each other,

00:00:56.440 --> 00:01:03.430
namima sasurau nanpasen no you ni

00:00:56.440 --> 00:01:03.430
Like wrecked ships wandering on the waves...

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:08.870
mou nakanaide ima

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:08.870
Don't cry, any more,

00:01:08.870 --> 00:01:16.240
anata wo sagashite iru hito ga iru kara

00:01:08.870 --> 00:01:16.240
because now there is a person looking for you,

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:20.970
omae ni aitai yo to

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:20.970
Dying to see you...

00:01:30.250 --> 00:01:36.110
Colony Drop

00:02:01.050 --> 00:02:02.670
What?! They don't need to sortie?!

00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:06.910
<i>Mobile suits! Don't go yet!</i>

00:02:07.890 --> 00:02:10.050
<i>The mobile suit following us</i>
<i>is carrying a white flag.</i>

00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:11.690
A white flag?

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:19.230
I wish for permission to come on board.

00:02:19.300 --> 00:02:22.320
I have brought information
that will be useful to the A.E.U.G..

00:02:22.740 --> 00:02:25.070
<i>I wish for permission to come on board!</i>

00:02:43.960 --> 00:02:45.390
Okay, you're alone, are you?!

00:02:45.460 --> 00:02:46.390
Get off!

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:55.760
<i>So, you're saying the Titans went to</i>
<i>Side Four to prepare a colony drop?</i>

00:02:56.070 --> 00:02:57.760
That's what Sarah Zabiarov says.

00:02:58.940 --> 00:03:01.100
<i>Don't you think this could be a trap?</i>

00:03:01.510 --> 00:03:03.740
You can interpret this a
number of different ways...

00:03:03.810 --> 00:03:05.440
...but she's very young.

00:03:05.510 --> 00:03:09.850
It doesn't seem to be a lie that
she's grown sick of the Titans' ways.

00:03:10.250 --> 00:03:14.190
It's true that a colony from Side Four
is moving, right?

00:03:14.420 --> 00:03:16.410
<i>Yes, we have confirmation from Granada.</i>

00:03:16.490 --> 00:03:19.120
<i>However, we don't know where</i>
<i>it will hit the Moon!</i>

00:03:19.330 --> 00:03:21.990
But this girl, Sarah, is saying
it'll fall on Granada?!

00:03:22.700 --> 00:03:25.290
You said you trusted her information,
didn't you, Kamille?

00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:26.790
Y-Yes!

00:03:27.300 --> 00:03:29.930
In that case, let's believe
what the girl says.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:31.130
<i>Not Kamille again!</i>

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:33.000
<i>Being flattered that he's a Newtype...</i>

00:03:33.070 --> 00:03:34.800
<i>...giving us his unwanted opinions!</i>

00:03:35.370 --> 00:03:38.210
You will look after evacuating
the citizens of Granada, will you?

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:40.400
<i>I'll take care of things here in my way...</i>

00:03:40.480 --> 00:03:42.710
<i>...but dropping the colony</i>
<i>is a feint operation!</i>

00:03:42.780 --> 00:03:43.980
<i>The enemy's intents...!</i>

00:03:44.050 --> 00:03:45.810
The Argama will ensure the colony...

00:03:45.880 --> 00:03:46.980
...does not fall on the city!

00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:48.820
<i>Of course you will!</i>

00:03:49.050 --> 00:03:51.020
<i>Work together with the Radish</i>
<i>to achieve that objective.</i>

00:03:53.460 --> 00:03:55.620
Mr. Wong's perspective on this
is also correct.

00:03:55.690 --> 00:03:58.530
What could their true intentions be...

00:03:58.600 --> 00:04:00.570
...if dropping the colony
is only to distract our attention?

00:04:02.330 --> 00:04:04.500
An officer with a low rank
like myself couldn't answer that.

00:04:05.040 --> 00:04:07.030
All units, take level two battle stations!

00:04:07.110 --> 00:04:08.040
Yes, sir!

00:04:08.110 --> 00:04:09.630
You know how to use a lift grip,
don't you?

00:04:09.710 --> 00:04:10.870
- Yes, sir.
- Okay, then.

00:04:10.940 --> 00:04:12.740
- Right!
- Thanks!

00:04:25.290 --> 00:04:26.660
You'd be wise to behave.

00:04:26.730 --> 00:04:29.630
Once suspicions are cleared, you
can become a crewmember in no time.

00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:31.130
Thank you very much.

00:04:34.570 --> 00:04:36.160
Katz! No!

00:04:36.240 --> 00:04:37.960
She could still be an enemy!

00:04:38.040 --> 00:04:38.830
I'm here!

00:04:38.900 --> 00:04:40.500
Okay! Here's the key to this room!

00:04:40.570 --> 00:04:42.670
You could get in trouble again
if you stick around here.

00:04:43.310 --> 00:04:44.670
I know that.

00:04:52.650 --> 00:04:55.590
Who ordered you to jump
right into the lap of your enemy?

00:04:58.890 --> 00:05:03.390
You trusted my words
right from the beginning.

00:05:03.500 --> 00:05:04.890
Answer my question!

00:05:06.330 --> 00:05:08.770
I only believed this plan
to drop the colony.

00:05:08.830 --> 00:05:12.740
But it's still too hard to steal
a Hizack and escape the Titans.

00:05:12.810 --> 00:05:14.770
I risked my life to get here.

00:05:14.840 --> 00:05:18.140
I... I thought you were a pilot
that I could trust.

00:05:19.240 --> 00:05:22.210
Did he tell you that you could
trick people if you said that?

00:05:22.450 --> 00:05:24.420
No! Scirocco only...!

00:05:24.720 --> 00:05:26.650
Paptimus Scirocco.

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:29.410
The captain of the Jupitris
who just returned from Jupiter.

00:05:29.760 --> 00:05:30.810
No, you're wrong!

00:05:30.890 --> 00:05:34.120
You're underestimating the A.E.U.G.'s
intelligence network.

00:05:34.430 --> 00:05:38.730
I mean, no, it's the ways of Jamaican
that I could no longer bear!

00:05:38.800 --> 00:05:41.100
To go ahead with a colony drop operation...

00:05:41.170 --> 00:05:43.760
...annihilating Granada even without
using nuclear weapons.

00:05:44.540 --> 00:05:48.130
He's planning to kill millions of people
who have done nothing wrong.

00:05:51.780 --> 00:05:56.270
If the colony drop succeeds, will that
inconvenience Scirocco in any way?

00:05:57.780 --> 00:05:59.750
Are you a Cyber-Newtype?

00:06:04.990 --> 00:06:06.720
That girl is dangerous.

00:06:06.790 --> 00:06:09.780
But I understand Cyber-Newtypes
are emotionally unstable.

00:06:10.400 --> 00:06:11.760
She doesn't look that way to me.

00:06:11.830 --> 00:06:15.390
Yeah, I hope she becomes an ally.

00:06:15.470 --> 00:06:17.770
However, we've got to test her
thoroughly first.

00:06:18.840 --> 00:06:20.460
That was a test?!

00:06:36.860 --> 00:06:39.880
We can adjust the course by using the
nuclear pulses twice, right?

00:06:40.190 --> 00:06:42.020
Yes, we're on track.

00:06:42.090 --> 00:06:47.030
What an easy way
to totally stop the A.E.U.G..

00:06:47.100 --> 00:06:49.070
It's a plan not even Scirocco
would've thought of.

00:06:49.670 --> 00:06:50.930
I believe Scirocco's...

00:06:51.000 --> 00:06:54.960
...trying to release his frustrations
of his return from Jupiter through battle.

00:06:55.040 --> 00:06:56.740
You're right about that.

00:06:56.810 --> 00:06:58.740
The reason we retreated
from Von Braun City...

00:06:58.810 --> 00:07:00.570
...so shortly after occupying it...

00:07:00.650 --> 00:07:03.310
...is because he'd kept going in
and coming out so selfishly.

00:07:03.380 --> 00:07:07.550
The Alexandria cannot return
to Gryps until we redeem our honor here.

00:07:13.530 --> 00:07:18.020
It's the 27th Colony of Side Four's
colony group that's begun to move.

00:07:18.360 --> 00:07:20.330
You're certain it's uninhabited,
aren't you?

00:07:20.700 --> 00:07:22.500
- Sorry I'm late.
- Hi!

00:07:22.630 --> 00:07:25.260
I'm still not used to the decks
of the Radish.

00:07:25.340 --> 00:07:27.860
What the girl who boarded
the Argama says is true.

00:07:28.340 --> 00:07:30.330
We can think of several courses.

00:07:30.780 --> 00:07:32.870
Dropping it on Granada
is certainly a possibility.

00:07:33.550 --> 00:07:34.940
What's the enemy's battle strength?

00:07:35.010 --> 00:07:36.670
They're trying not to be noticed...

00:07:36.750 --> 00:07:38.010
...so their force can't be too great.

00:07:38.080 --> 00:07:41.020
But enough of a force
to carry the nuclear pulses...

00:07:41.090 --> 00:07:42.880
...needed to move the colony, right?

00:07:45.020 --> 00:07:48.890
R-Right.
It'll be a dangerous mission for you.

00:07:51.700 --> 00:07:55.130
The Titans will use their nuclear pulse
when they want to change its course.

00:07:55.200 --> 00:07:56.790
I'm worried about
radioactive contamination.

00:07:56.870 --> 00:07:59.360
I'll be okay as long as I don't leave
the Gundam's cockpit.

00:07:59.440 --> 00:08:02.700
However, if as a result
you're no longer able to bear children...!

00:08:02.770 --> 00:08:06.510
I-I have no intention... of getting married.

00:08:06.580 --> 00:08:08.410
Lieutenant Emma!

00:08:15.190 --> 00:08:16.920
Boy, that was awkward.

00:08:18.620 --> 00:08:22.920
<i>Kamille believed that girl who</i>
<i>defected right from the beginning.</i>

00:08:30.640 --> 00:08:32.040
Oh, my.

00:08:32.800 --> 00:08:34.900
I will be proposed to in the near future?!

00:08:45.620 --> 00:08:47.280
I'm taking the captain's meal to him.

00:08:47.350 --> 00:08:49.840
- Oh, can you wait a moment?
- Sure.

00:08:50.420 --> 00:08:53.650
- Return this to the person in charge.
- Okay!

00:09:01.170 --> 00:09:04.030
Don't get too close to that girl, Katz.

00:09:04.100 --> 00:09:05.660
Why is it okay for you...

00:09:05.740 --> 00:09:07.500
...and not okay for me, Kamille?

00:09:09.680 --> 00:09:10.770
Katz.

00:09:10.840 --> 00:09:12.810
Kamille is cautioning you.

00:09:13.180 --> 00:09:14.770
But he's not my superior.

00:09:15.280 --> 00:09:19.680
I wonder how Mr. Amuro
would react if he heard that.

00:09:19.750 --> 00:09:20.980
That has nothing to do with it.

00:09:21.050 --> 00:09:23.080
Besides, we're not even on Earth.

00:09:28.930 --> 00:09:31.690
I hear you suddenly get serious
when it comes to that girl.

00:09:31.760 --> 00:09:34.130
Sarah, the one who defected.

00:09:34.200 --> 00:09:36.170
Did Katz tell you that?

00:09:36.230 --> 00:09:38.000
You went into her room alone, didn't you?

00:09:38.370 --> 00:09:39.430
Big deal.

00:09:39.500 --> 00:09:40.230
Kamille!

00:09:40.910 --> 00:09:42.530
What's with the third degree?!

00:09:42.610 --> 00:09:45.510
You're not a member
of the intelligence bureau!

00:09:45.980 --> 00:09:48.910
It's not your job
to interrogate defectors!

00:09:48.980 --> 00:09:50.310
Of course not!

00:09:50.380 --> 00:09:53.870
Then should you be entering that girl
Sarah's room alone...

00:09:53.950 --> 00:09:55.390
...and closing the door behind you?!

00:09:55.920 --> 00:09:57.510
I-I guess... not.

00:09:57.590 --> 00:09:59.560
I was mistaken.

00:09:59.990 --> 00:10:00.920
I apologize.

00:10:00.990 --> 00:10:02.890
Well, did something happen
between you and Sarah?!

00:10:02.960 --> 00:10:03.990
Of course not!

00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:09.090
Coffee?

00:10:09.170 --> 00:10:11.530
- No, thank you.
- Okay.

00:10:11.740 --> 00:10:13.710
This could be the last meal
I'll have in peace.

00:10:14.210 --> 00:10:16.200
I don't like what you're implying.

00:10:16.510 --> 00:10:18.810
The enemy has ordered a child
to sneak in here.

00:10:18.880 --> 00:10:20.870
So, as young as she is, she's a spy?

00:10:21.850 --> 00:10:25.780
When using a Newtype for battle,
age is irrelevant.

00:10:26.180 --> 00:10:28.020
Well, that may be true, but...!

00:10:28.090 --> 00:10:30.020
I've sent Lieutenant Emma to the Radish.

00:10:30.090 --> 00:10:31.580
So, I'm a little worried.

00:10:31.660 --> 00:10:33.560
Kamille's handling things well.

00:10:33.630 --> 00:10:35.220
Even with Fa nagging at him.

00:10:35.760 --> 00:10:39.030
Yes, he's begun to grow more cautious
with his intuition.

00:10:39.100 --> 00:10:40.720
However, he's still very young.

00:10:41.400 --> 00:10:43.530
I thought age is irrelevant with Newtypes.

00:10:44.240 --> 00:10:46.200
I don't believe he's a Newtype, yet.

00:10:46.300 --> 00:10:48.070
Because he has a short temper?

00:10:48.310 --> 00:10:50.270
Yeah, like myself.

00:10:58.020 --> 00:10:59.880
- You've located it?!
- Yes!

00:10:59.950 --> 00:11:01.940
There's a colony ahead of us
headed for the Moon!

00:11:02.590 --> 00:11:03.710
Okay.

00:11:03.790 --> 00:11:05.350
It's one of two possibilities.

00:11:05.420 --> 00:11:08.360
They're either planning to drop it
on Von Braun or on Granada.

00:11:08.430 --> 00:11:10.120
I take it the Argama's already aware of this!

00:11:11.000 --> 00:11:13.060
Why can't it be calculated?!

00:11:13.130 --> 00:11:14.100
Okay!

00:11:14.230 --> 00:11:16.200
The warnings we send out are different...

00:11:16.270 --> 00:11:18.290
...depending on if it's directed at
Granada or Von Braun!

00:11:18.370 --> 00:11:19.300
Hurry!

00:11:19.370 --> 00:11:21.400
Have the mobile suit team on standby!

00:11:21.470 --> 00:11:22.440
Yes, sir!

00:11:28.810 --> 00:11:31.040
<i>An enemy battleship detected ahead of us.</i>

00:11:31.120 --> 00:11:32.340
<i>Mobile suit team!</i>

00:11:32.420 --> 00:11:35.750
<i>Except for those protecting the colony,</i>
<i>prepare for battle against enemy suits!</i>

00:11:35.820 --> 00:11:37.120
<i>If this plan succeeds...</i>

00:11:37.190 --> 00:11:39.590
<i>...all will receive a one-week paid vacation.</i>

00:11:39.660 --> 00:11:41.420
<i>I expect all units to give it their everything!</i>

00:11:41.490 --> 00:11:43.980
We retreat from Von Braun, and as soon
as we get resupplied...

00:11:44.060 --> 00:11:45.030
...we're to fight again!

00:11:45.460 --> 00:11:47.190
Are we Jamaican's toys?!

00:11:47.530 --> 00:11:48.330
<i>Yazan.</i>

00:11:48.400 --> 00:11:51.130
<i>Don't expect the feelings of one pilot</i>
<i>to make any changes to our plan!</i>

00:11:51.600 --> 00:11:53.590
Then let me try a frontal attack!

00:11:53.670 --> 00:11:55.300
<i>I'm not saying you can't fight!</i>

00:11:55.740 --> 00:11:58.770
<i>Take a moment to figure out</i>
<i>why I made you a squadron leader!</i>

00:11:58.840 --> 00:11:59.710
All right.

00:12:18.500 --> 00:12:21.230
Although there still is some distance,
mobile suit team...!

00:12:21.300 --> 00:12:23.230
- Take off now, in order!
- Yes, sir!

00:12:23.300 --> 00:12:25.460
Be careful, Tripper!

00:12:25.540 --> 00:12:26.500
<i>Roger!</i>

00:12:26.940 --> 00:12:28.670
I'm going ahead, Lieutenant Apolly!

00:12:28.740 --> 00:12:30.000
<i>Okay, go!</i>

00:12:40.390 --> 00:12:42.250
There's a lot of commotion
going on outside.

00:12:42.320 --> 00:12:45.290
Yeah, the mobile suits
have begun to take off.

00:12:45.860 --> 00:12:47.620
I have no weapon.
Are you afraid of me?

00:12:48.430 --> 00:12:50.520
I'll bet you're a black belt
in karate or something.

00:12:50.600 --> 00:12:52.390
That's too barbarous for me!

00:12:52.960 --> 00:12:54.400
I've been taking lessons.

00:12:54.670 --> 00:12:55.690
Here.

00:12:57.200 --> 00:12:58.600
Isn't it too big?

00:12:58.670 --> 00:13:02.540
If the measurements you disclosed
about yourself are correct, it should be fine.

00:13:02.610 --> 00:13:04.400
I guess because it's the cheaper one.

00:13:04.940 --> 00:13:06.600
By the way, should you be here right now?

00:13:07.180 --> 00:13:08.510
What do you mean?

00:13:08.580 --> 00:13:10.140
You're a pilot, right?

00:13:10.220 --> 00:13:12.050
Shouldn't you be taking off?

00:13:12.150 --> 00:13:15.020
Even if I wanted to,
there aren't enough mobile suits.

00:13:15.620 --> 00:13:17.450
You've got my Hizack.

00:13:17.720 --> 00:13:19.310
Your Hizack?

00:13:19.390 --> 00:13:20.520
Not that model.

00:13:20.590 --> 00:13:24.120
I've tried out a number of Zeon types,
but I've never even touched the Hizack.

00:13:24.630 --> 00:13:25.600
I see.

00:13:30.870 --> 00:13:31.890
Thank you.

00:13:31.970 --> 00:13:34.460
I should be able to survive
a little longer with this, Katz.

00:13:36.110 --> 00:13:37.370
I only followed captain's orders.

00:13:38.080 --> 00:13:40.840
But you're the one who brought it to me!

00:13:42.180 --> 00:13:43.480
Thank you.

00:13:43.620 --> 00:13:44.780
S-Sure.

00:13:46.320 --> 00:13:49.380
I'd be able to teach you
how to pilot that Hizack.

00:13:49.450 --> 00:13:50.720
You, Sarah?

00:13:50.790 --> 00:13:54.850
We could get to the mobile suit deck
if it looked like you were taking me there.

00:13:55.630 --> 00:13:56.720
I-I get it.

00:13:56.800 --> 00:13:59.090
You're a Newtype, right?

00:13:59.160 --> 00:14:02.460
I would love to see you battle.

00:14:04.340 --> 00:14:05.130
Y-Yeah, sure thing.

00:14:08.010 --> 00:14:08.940
Okay, then.

00:14:09.010 --> 00:14:11.530
- Put on your helmet and get in front of me.
- Okay.

00:14:16.410 --> 00:14:19.380
Even the Gundam Mk. II
is not almighty, you know!

00:14:19.580 --> 00:14:21.680
I'll make sure it can be used
before the next operation!

00:14:22.250 --> 00:14:25.590
I might not be able to get back
without the G-Defenser!

00:14:26.060 --> 00:14:27.750
Don't frighten me!

00:14:27.830 --> 00:14:29.290
But it's true!

00:14:30.460 --> 00:14:33.090
Darn it!
Making me work my butt off, and this?!

00:14:33.160 --> 00:14:34.320
<i>I'm sorry, Lieutenant.</i>

00:14:35.000 --> 00:14:37.090
<i>I'll have it made operational</i>
<i>before you return.</i>

00:14:37.170 --> 00:14:38.600
<i>We'll go get you with the Radish!</i>

00:14:39.500 --> 00:14:42.130
<i>You mustn't die!</i>
<i>You'd make everyone unhappy.</i>

00:14:43.610 --> 00:14:45.540
Emma! Gundam Mk. II! Taking off!

00:14:52.350 --> 00:14:53.720
Reccoa! Methuss! Taking off!

00:14:58.860 --> 00:15:00.980
Kamille! Zeta Gundam! Let's do it!

00:15:24.080 --> 00:15:25.110
Yes.

00:15:25.180 --> 00:15:27.880
We mustn't say anything
that could cause public disturbances.

00:15:32.360 --> 00:15:33.980
I'm off the line!

00:15:34.130 --> 00:15:36.620
He's asking if it isn't time we
started evacuating the citizens?

00:15:36.690 --> 00:15:37.350
Who's asking?!

00:15:37.430 --> 00:15:39.520
- The Mayor of Granada...!
- Wong!

00:15:40.130 --> 00:15:42.260
I'm tired of your talk of
the A.E.U.G.'s war tactics!

00:15:42.330 --> 00:15:44.030
I'll evacuate the citizens
to the underground tunnel!

00:15:44.100 --> 00:15:45.540
You mustn't!

00:15:45.600 --> 00:15:47.540
Even Melanie Hue Carbine says...

00:15:47.670 --> 00:15:49.970
...to leave it to the Argama and Radish!

00:15:50.340 --> 00:15:52.310
But what if something should happen
to the citizens?

00:15:52.510 --> 00:15:55.540
Please have trust in the battle strength
of the forces we created.

00:15:56.080 --> 00:15:57.840
They're taking forever
to make a move!

00:15:57.920 --> 00:15:59.140
No, they're not!

00:15:59.220 --> 00:16:01.810
It's the lives of Granada's citizens
we're talking about!

00:16:01.950 --> 00:16:02.920
Mr. Mayor.

00:16:03.390 --> 00:16:05.320
Both the Argama and Radish will win.

00:16:05.590 --> 00:16:07.520
If not, Earth will be destroyed...

00:16:07.590 --> 00:16:09.790
...and that will be it
for the Titans and A.E.U.G..

00:16:09.860 --> 00:16:11.620
That's true, but...!

00:16:11.700 --> 00:16:14.220
Therefore, the A.E.U.G. will win.

00:16:14.470 --> 00:16:18.160
I'm certain. That's why I beg you not
to stage an evacuation...

00:16:18.240 --> 00:16:22.570
...that might cause the citizens
to doubt the A.E.U.G.'s abilities.

00:16:23.310 --> 00:16:24.940
Please.

00:16:25.010 --> 00:16:27.380
You're saying if they fail,
we'll all be dead anyway.

00:16:45.430 --> 00:16:46.520
Target confirmed!

00:16:46.600 --> 00:16:48.070
Main cannon!
You know what to do?!

00:16:48.130 --> 00:16:51.100
<i>Change its course!</i>
<i>Aim to the left of the target!</i>

00:16:51.170 --> 00:16:52.640
<i>I'm not some kid you're talking to!</i>

00:16:53.140 --> 00:16:55.070
I'm going to change the course
of the colony!

00:16:55.470 --> 00:16:57.340
Once you fire the main cannon,
the enemy will fire back!

00:16:57.780 --> 00:16:59.270
Increase to level one battle speed!

00:16:59.340 --> 00:17:00.280
Yes, sir!

00:17:00.350 --> 00:17:01.610
Main cannon!

00:17:04.120 --> 00:17:05.410
It's begun!

00:17:12.990 --> 00:17:15.120
Fire at the origin of the firing line!

00:17:15.790 --> 00:17:17.560
Where's Yazan gone to, since he took off?!

00:17:21.600 --> 00:17:24.230
You're planning on coming
from above the colony, right?

00:17:25.200 --> 00:17:26.640
I can read your moves!

00:17:29.310 --> 00:17:30.300
Over there!

00:17:36.310 --> 00:17:38.580
I won't let the A.E.U.G. continue
to have it their way!

00:17:40.350 --> 00:17:41.510
What's the matter, Katz?!

00:17:42.050 --> 00:17:45.150
Y-Yes! I'm told the Hizack's
in the way on the catapult deck.

00:17:45.220 --> 00:17:46.490
Orders from the bridge?

00:17:46.560 --> 00:17:48.490
We've got a battle between vessels
going out there!

00:17:48.560 --> 00:17:50.530
Mechanics, get to the gun platforms
and fight!

00:17:57.870 --> 00:17:59.340
Is it going to work?!

00:17:59.470 --> 00:18:01.130
At this rate, the colony
will not fall on Granada!

00:18:01.610 --> 00:18:02.870
It's all right!

00:18:02.940 --> 00:18:04.430
It's too big!

00:18:04.510 --> 00:18:08.070
It'll keep straight as long as
the nuclear pulse engine isn't activated!

00:18:10.080 --> 00:18:12.950
Is that the mobile armor that assaulted Fa?

00:18:15.120 --> 00:18:19.250
Reccoa is fighting mobile suits? Then I'll
tend to the nuclear pulse engine!

00:18:26.360 --> 00:18:27.730
Get out of my way!

00:18:35.870 --> 00:18:37.170
Huh? Did you say something?

00:18:37.880 --> 00:18:42.140
The transforming mobile suit from
the Alexandria has a blind spot.

00:18:42.210 --> 00:18:44.370
What? But it uses a panoramic
monitor, doesn't it?

00:18:44.520 --> 00:18:45.880
There's a section it can't see?

00:18:45.950 --> 00:18:46.920
Yes.

00:18:47.050 --> 00:18:49.680
Because, apparently,
it was made in a hurry.

00:18:49.750 --> 00:18:51.620
- Below.
- I see...!

00:18:51.990 --> 00:18:53.890
You're... very nice.

00:18:53.960 --> 00:18:54.690
Huh?

00:18:54.760 --> 00:18:56.490
I'm glad to have met you.

00:19:02.270 --> 00:19:04.360
I mean what I'm saying, Katz.

00:19:04.440 --> 00:19:05.830
I like you.

00:19:08.640 --> 00:19:09.540
That damn girl!

00:19:12.240 --> 00:19:15.210
That girl! That girl!

00:19:15.280 --> 00:19:16.710
That damn girl!

00:19:16.780 --> 00:19:18.370
<i>She was a spy, after all!</i>

00:19:18.450 --> 00:19:19.280
Katz!

00:19:19.350 --> 00:19:21.480
You shouldn't be there! It's dangerous!

00:19:21.550 --> 00:19:23.350
It was not my intention to let her escape!

00:19:23.420 --> 00:19:24.680
What?

00:19:24.760 --> 00:19:25.720
Are you saying...

00:19:25.790 --> 00:19:27.220
...you let Sarah get away?!

00:19:35.230 --> 00:19:36.630
This has become a dogfight!

00:19:39.670 --> 00:19:40.570
I-It's strong!

00:19:42.240 --> 00:19:43.170
You're going to fall!

00:19:48.880 --> 00:19:50.250
You still fight like a child!

00:19:52.280 --> 00:19:53.340
It's strong!

00:19:53.850 --> 00:19:56.010
I'll ram these through you
from the outside!

00:19:59.890 --> 00:20:02.360
- Not done yet!
- <i>Attack from below! Can you hear me?!</i>

00:20:02.430 --> 00:20:03.690
From below?! That makes sense!

00:20:08.670 --> 00:20:10.130
I can't see it!

00:20:12.600 --> 00:20:13.230
This'll hit!

00:20:17.780 --> 00:20:19.210
Zeta, I think its name is!

00:20:19.280 --> 00:20:21.270
Does it know the weak point
of this machine?!

00:20:25.320 --> 00:20:29.150
If I can ignite this nuclear pulse
to change the direction of the colony...!

00:20:31.790 --> 00:20:33.150
Don't get in my way!

00:20:41.530 --> 00:20:43.500
With the use of this worn out engine...!

00:20:54.710 --> 00:20:55.840
I did it!

00:21:03.620 --> 00:21:05.520
The colony's course has changed!

00:21:05.590 --> 00:21:07.110
What is Yazan doing?!

00:21:07.190 --> 00:21:08.590
Mobile suit team, returning!

00:21:08.990 --> 00:21:11.020
The direction can no longer be changed.

00:21:11.100 --> 00:21:12.260
This plan...!

00:21:12.700 --> 00:21:15.130
Thanks to the pressure
we applied through battle...

00:21:15.200 --> 00:21:18.400
...Lt. Emma getting the engine going,
we managed to change its direction.

00:21:18.470 --> 00:21:19.300
Yes.

00:21:19.370 --> 00:21:23.170
So, it'll now take this course,
and hit here, right?

00:21:25.540 --> 00:21:28.840
It will unquestionably fall
180 kilometers away from Granada.

00:21:28.910 --> 00:21:29.610
What a relief.

00:22:02.210 --> 00:22:05.180
You saved me by telling me about
the enemy's blind spot, Katz, but...

00:22:06.020 --> 00:22:07.110
I understand.

00:22:07.190 --> 00:22:09.780
Think about what you did wrong. Got that?

00:22:09.850 --> 00:22:11.340
And remain in that seated position.

00:22:11.720 --> 00:22:12.690
Yes.

00:22:22.370 --> 00:22:26.170
Are humans... that difficult to trust?

00:22:47.270 --> 00:22:49.600
Oh, I can't help believing you

00:22:50.480 --> 00:22:56.020
kanarazu aeru to ano hi kara shinjiteita

00:22:50.480 --> 00:22:56.020
I've believed we're sure to meet again ever since that day

00:22:56.070 --> 00:23:01.400
kitto yobiau kokoro ga areba

00:22:56.070 --> 00:23:01.400
If we have heart, we'll be called together again

00:23:01.450 --> 00:23:11.790
mugen no Energy yobisamasu

00:23:01.450 --> 00:23:11.790
Awaken the infinite energy

00:23:11.830 --> 00:23:17.420
aa kizutsukeau mae ni

00:23:11.830 --> 00:23:17.420
Before you get hurt

00:23:17.460 --> 00:23:23.510
dekiru koto sagashite Please

00:23:17.460 --> 00:23:23.510
Find what you can do...Please

00:23:23.550 --> 00:23:28.680
nagedasanai de kurushii toki koso

00:23:23.550 --> 00:23:28.680
Don't throw it away because of this painful age

00:23:29.390 --> 00:23:32.020
itsuka mita aoi sora wo

00:23:29.390 --> 00:23:32.020
Until the day we gaze up again

00:23:32.030 --> 00:23:39.030
kitto anata to miageru hi made

00:23:32.030 --> 00:23:39.030
at the blue sky we once saw

00:23:44.580 --> 00:23:47.910
Yazan takes the first steps
toward a relentless antagonism.

00:23:47.990 --> 00:23:49.950
But mixed within the battle zone...

00:23:50.020 --> 00:23:53.110
...is a battleship belonging to
the former Principality of Zeon.

00:23:53.190 --> 00:23:58.180
While there, Katz discovers a weapon with
the ability to destroy Yazan's mobile suit.

00:23:58.730 --> 00:24:02.690
Are people being chased by
the ghosts of Zeon?

00:24:02.900 --> 00:24:07.500
Next on Mobile Suit Zeta Gundam,
"The Ghost of Zeon".

00:24:07.460 --> 00:24:12.440
Next Episode

00:24:07.460 --> 00:24:12.440
The Ghost of Zeon

00:24:08.010 --> 00:24:10.570
You will see the tears of time.
